<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>BBC News</title><subtitle type="html">BBC News - Technology</subtitle><id>https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:46:05Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss.xml" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/technology" /><link rel="via" href="https://feeds.bbci.co.uk/news/technology/rss.xml" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Could robots be the future of theme parks?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cdr7g3vdl58o#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:46:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T02:02:02Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cdr7g3vdl58o--17cf8c14f1b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cdr7g3vdl58o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Galaxy Robot Park is a 16,500-square-meter venue in South Korea, with attractions including humanoid robots dancing to K-pop hits.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI data centres are booming in Australia - but at what cost?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgl3we7wdr3o#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T18:32:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgl3we7wdr3o--8b5b6bafacff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cgl3we7wdr3o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Advocates say data centres will bring jobs but others worry they will suck up resources while providing little advantage.</summary></entry><entry><title>Nvidia strikes $12.9bn deal to buy AI platform Hugging Face</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr4vnr5g1k7o#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T16:32:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr4vnr5g1k7o--ea12f1547314.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cr4vnr5g1k7o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The deal gives Nvidia control of a leading open-source AI platform and developer community.</summary></entry><entry><title>Watch: BBC travels in self-driving Uber around London</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwyzeyd7peeo#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T07:20:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwyzeyd7peeo--14d7e8146377.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/cwyzeyd7peeo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The BBC's Zoe Kleinman takes a ride on Uber's self-driving robotaxi as the service rolls out on Thursday.</summary></entry><entry><title>Uber launches UK's first robotaxis with a driver - here's what it's like to ride in one</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ce9e838jzpzo#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T23:36:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ce9e838jzpzo--7c5ce206b2d3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/ce9e838jzpzo?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The ride-hailing app has launched 15 self-driving taxis, but they will have safety drivers inside.</summary></entry><entry><title>Uber to cut over 3,000 jobs in major global restructuring</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cp3ky2w4y9no#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T16:51:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cp3ky2w4y9no--b25463dd89fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cp3ky2w4y9no?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The company says cutting roles would make its operations "simpler and faster".</summary></entry><entry><title>Lords call for AI 'kill switch' powers in UK</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn9wv80j9w9o#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T14:41:52Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn9wv80j9w9o--6e63ea3a2535.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cn9wv80j9w9o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Its backers say it would provide a "vital safety net" against runaway AI systems such as those from OpenAI and Anthropic.</summary></entry><entry><title>Criminals publish data of 8.7m people after airports hack</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c74k39g3ee5o#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T11:00:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c74k39g3ee5o--3037c2ce91ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c74k39g3ee5o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The company, which owns Manchester, Stansted and East Midlands airports, was hacked last month.</summary></entry><entry><title>Fake 10 Downing Street listing exposes 'unfit' Booking.com, says consumer group</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cly4e0wn452o#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T01:27:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cly4e0wn452o--a9332f97bc35.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cly4e0wn452o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Booking.com said the "limited test" was "not a true reflection of the experience of millions of listings or reviews".</summary></entry><entry><title>Will self-flying planes transform the skies?</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1l123mmrg7o#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T23:27:35Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1l123mmrg7o--d0b97e38a85d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c1l123mmrg7o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Autonomous crop-spraying aircraft are leading the way in pilot-free flying.</summary></entry><entry><title>AI could cause global economic downturn, Andrew Bailey warns G20</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c99dym3prl1o#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:18:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c99dym3prl1o--5a66c59ca107.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c99dym3prl1o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">The governor of the Bank of England warned of AI's “volatility” caused by energy shocks from the US-Iran war.</summary></entry><entry><title>Amazon rigged $20bn worth of ad prices, US lawsuit alleges</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvgy91nvy27o#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T21:28:49Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvgy91nvy27o--f08abcf946bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cvgy91nvy27o?at_medium=RSS&amp;at_campaign=rss" /><summary type="html">Amazon responded to the lawsuit, arguing the US Federal Trade Commission "misunderstands" their ad market.</summary></entry><entry><title>I've been to Gamescom six times - here's what excited me this year</title><id>https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cew92lp2g45o#0</id><updated>2026-09-04T04:45:05Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T23:02:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cew92lp2g45o--5d7564af3869.html" type="text/